{uses:..\3_0-preface.lbl}
' i.test esc: try the C128 screen editor's Esc sequences on the caller's
' screen (11/11/2026, a prototype for ++ visual: modules/TODO.md, "C128
' screen-editor escapes"). For each: lines "1abcdefghij".."6abcdefghij",
' the cursor put on the "d" of the 3 line (&,70,4,4), Esc and the letter,
' then "*"; what it should look like is said below, and the caller answers
' Yes or No (im 96). A summary at the end; nothing is saved.
'
' The sysop's console is checked without anyone watching by
' tools/esctest.py (tests/standin/esc.bas): all ten work there, in 40 and
' 80 columns, the mask on or off; Esc T/B (a window) doesn't, as Image
' does its own carriage returns and cursor placing, so it's left out here.
'
' Run it as a module: R at the main prompt, class 3, "test esc".
' For a caller in Commodore translation only: Esc codes mean nothing to an
' ASCII terminal (flag 16 set).
{alpha:alt}
{include:..\quoters.lbl}
{:3000}
	pr$="i."+"test esc":rem "i.test esc" {usedef:__BuildDate} {usedef:__BuildTime}
	cm$="Esc Test"+"":gosub 9:&,52,16,3:if a%=. then {:esc_ok}
	&"{f6}These are Commodore 128 screen codes{colon} switch{f6}to Commodore translation (AT1) first.{f6}":goto 300
{:esc_ok}
	&,18,0:&"{clear}{f6}{white}This shows the C128 screen editor's Esc{f6}codes{comma} one at a time. After each{comma} say{f6}whether your screen looked as described.{f6:2}"
	&"A C128 in 128 mode with a terminal that{f6}passes them on should do them all.{f6:2}Ready{question} ":gosub 96:if a=. then {:esc_end}
	es$=chr$(27):b$="":restore
	for t=1 to 10:read l$,n$,d$
	&"{clear}{white}Esc "+l$+"{colon} "+n$:for r=1 to 6:&,70,0,r+1:&mid$(str$(r),2)+"abcdefghij":next
	&,70,4,4:a$=es$+l$:&:&"*":&,70,0,12:&"{lt. blue}Expected{colon} "+d$+"{f6:2}{white}Did it look like that{question} ":gosub 96
	b$=b$+mid$("NY",a+1,1):next
	&"{clear}{white}Esc codes on your screen{colon}{f6:2}":restore:for t=1 to 10:read l$,n$,d$
	&"{lt. blue}Esc "+l$+"  "+left$(n$+"{space:24}",24)+"{white}"+mid$("No Yes",3*-(mid$(b$,t,1)="Y")+1,3)+"{f6}":next
	&"{f6}Computer type{colon} "+co$+"{f6:2}Hit a key{colon} {pound}g1"
{:esc_end}
	&,18,1:goto 300
' the tests: the letter (lower case: built as $41-$5a, the unshifted key, as
' the stand-in sends it; "Q" would be $d1), what it does, what it should show
	data "q","Erase to end of line","the 3 line is 3abc* (the rest erased)"
	data "p","Erase to start of line","the 3 line is four blanks{comma} *efghij"
	data "@","Erase to end of screen","3abc*{comma} and the 4-6 lines erased"
	data "j","Cursor to line start","the 3 line is *abcdefghij"
	data "k","Cursor to line end","the 3 line is 3abcdefghij*"
	data "i","Insert a line","a blank line with *{comma} 3-6 below it"
	data "d","Delete a line","the 3 line gone{comma} *abcdefghij in its place"
	data "v","Scroll up","all up one{comma} the 4 line is 4abc*efghij"
	data "w","Scroll down","all down one{comma} the 2 line is 2abc*efghij"
	data "o","Cancel modes","no change{comma} the 3 line is 3abc*efghij"
